# This is NOT a file to copy onto the box anymore. The box's /opt/binxportal/.env
# is generated on every deploy (see deploy/redeploy.sh) from AWS Secrets
# Manager — the secret `binxportal/app` in us-east-2, one JSON blob (see
# infra/lib/secrets-stack.ts). This file just documents that blob's shape,
# and the placeholder values CDK creates it with (which then get overwritten
# via `aws secretsmanager put-secret-value` — never committed, never set by
# CDK itself):
#
# {
#   "POSTGRES_PASSWORD": "...",   openssl rand -hex 32
#   "JWT_SECRET": "...",          openssl rand -hex 32
#   "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY": "...",   blank is fine — AI features fail gracefully
#   "NEXT_SERVER_ACTIONS_ENCRYPTION_KEY": "..."   openssl rand -base64 32
# }
#
# To update a value:
#   aws secretsmanager get-secret-value --secret-id binxportal/app --region us-east-2 \
#     --query SecretString --output text | jq '.JWT_SECRET = "new-value"' \
#     | aws secretsmanager put-secret-value --secret-id binxportal/app --region us-east-2 \
#     --secret-string file:///dev/stdin
# ...then redeploy (bash deploy/redeploy.sh via SSM, or just push) to pick it up.
#
# API_IMAGE / WEB_IMAGE aren't secrets and aren't in here — deploy/redeploy.sh
# computes them directly from the known ECR registry/repo names.
